  "assertions": [
    "begin/end marker event counts are 1/0",
    "all event PCs map to a real ELF instruction",
    "O3 six files byte-identical to O2 and to both frozen references",
    "two independent profile runs produce byte-identical CSVs",
    "MVE signed I8 dot opcode events identical in O2 and O3 (arithmetic unchanged)"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Guest instruction events are not cycles. No DWT/cycle model, pipeline calibration, memory wait, cache or external-memory cost is included.",
    "Cortex-M55 is in-order; only specific 16-bit Thumb-1 pairs can dual issue and MVE operations take two 64-bit beats, so real latency is above the naive 1-instruction-per-cycle figure, not below it.",
    "objdump aliases several MVE opcodes as coprocessor instructions, so the mnemonic class split is partial; function attribution comes from ELF labels and is complete.",
    "QEMU host wall seconds in the RESULT.json files are emulation time and are never used as chip latency."
  ]
}
